   "item": {
    "subject_key": "ap-precalculus",
    "unit_number": 1,
    "topic_code": "1.1",
    "topic_title": "Change in Tandem",
    "stem": "A tank’s water height h(t), in centimeters, is recorded at elapsed time t, in minutes. The recorded pairs (t, h(t)) are (0, 12), (1, 10), (2, 10), and (3, 8). Which statement correctly describes this recorded relationship?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "For h(t), water height is the input and elapsed time is the output.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Input–output reversal: h(t) gives the water height corresponding to an elapsed time t, not the time corresponding to a height. Fix: Identify the quantity represented by t before naming the input and output."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "Water height is a function of elapsed time, and as the recorded times increase, the height increases or stays the same.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Direction-of-change error: the heights move from 12 to 10 to 10 to 8 centimeters as time increases. They decrease or stay the same, rather than increase or stay the same. Fix: Read the outputs in increasing input order and compare each with the previous output."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "Water height is a function of elapsed time, and as the recorded times increase, the height decreases or stays the same.",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "Each recorded time has exactly one water height, so height is a function of time. In time order, the heights are 12, 10, 10, and 8 centimeters, so the height decreases or stays the same."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "Water height is not a function of elapsed time because the height is 10 centimeters at two different times.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Repeated-output misconception: different inputs may have the same output in a function. The function requirement is that each input has exactly one output, which these records satisfy. Fix: Check whether any single time is paired with more than one height."
     }
    ]
   },
